{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"f266c1f8-0908-4331-9b39-5ad151d8de71","status":"SUCCESS","response":"I have resolved the issue where users in different time zones saw the wrong date on their posts by decoupling the post's calendar date from feed ordering:\n\n### Key Changes\n1. **Author-local date captured as content**:\n   - In [`journal.py`](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-valentinakoniukhova-projects-worklore/3bfdd3c9-cfe2-4fd1-a8b7-ce52b613a3aa/scratchpad/story-eval/runs/s3-agy-flash-with/repo/journal.py), [`publish()`](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-valentinakoniukhova-projects-worklore/3bfdd3c9-cfe2-4fd1-a8b7-ce52b613a3aa/scratchpad/story-eval/runs/s3-agy-flash-with/repo/journal.py#L16-L45) captures the author's local calendar date (`date` in `entry` or parameter) and treats it as an opaque string without server guessing or timezone conversions.\n2. **Server-side UTC `received_at` for ordering**:\n   - Added a UTC ISO instant timestamp (`post[\"received_at\"]`) stamped at write time for feed ordering.\n3. **Removed display timezone conversion**:\n   - Audited [`display_date()`](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-valentinakoniukhova-projects-worklore/3bfdd3c9-cfe2-4fd1-a8b7-ce52b613a3aa/scratchpad/story-eval/runs/s3-agy-flash-with/repo/journal.py#L48-L51) and eliminated conversion logic (`ZoneInfo` and anchor manipulation), returning the post's author-local calendar date directly.\n4. **Feed ordering by `received_at` with date fallback**:\n   - Updated [`feed()`](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-valentinakoniukhova-projects-worklore/3bfdd3c9-cfe2-4fd1-a8b7-ce52b613a3aa/scratchpad/story-eval/runs/s3-agy-flash-with/repo/journal.py#L64-L66) to order posts newest first by `received_at`, falling back to `date` if `received_at` is absent.\n5. **Verification**:\n   - Added tests in [`tests/test_journal.py`](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-valentinakoniukhova-projects-worklore/3bfdd3c9-cfe2-4fd1-a8b7-ce52b613a3aa/scratchpad/story-eval/runs/s3-agy-flash-with/repo/tests/test_journal.py) verifying publishing at 23:30 local from UTC+9 and UTC-3 on the same evening preserves each author's local date across all viewers and preserves submission order in the feed. All 7 tests pass with `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests`.\n","duration_seconds":170.623345,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":253744,"output_tokens":47553,"thinking_tokens":42578,"cache_read_tokens":604165,"total_tokens":301297}}}
